    "headline_finding": "Ground truth (compiled voice-contract presence via faust -json, exact-match against llm/voice_contract.json's six accepted zone labels) reads 'effect' for all 19 corpus entries -- 0 of 19 contain any of gate/freq/key/gain/vel/velocity as a widget label, not even a partial contract. This is not because none of the prompts asked for an instrument (4 did, and the router correctly flagged all 4 as 'instrument' by wording alone); it is because every entry's stored `code` was generated by a pipeline that predates the voice-contract mechanism entirely and had no way to emit one. This corpus therefore CANNOT answer whether the router misroutes: it produces a 15/19 router/ground-truth agreement rate that is an artifact of corpus vintage, not a measurement of router accuracy, and must not be reported as one. The router's own dry-run agrees with the corpus's own hand-set `category` field on all 19 entries (its actual measurable behavior on this data); answering the real question requires either a corpus with post-2026-08-04 instrument-pipeline code, or a hand-labeled prompt-only ground truth independent of any generated code."
